[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   step_164: TEP-side generative model for the arrival anisotropy
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   (b130).
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   Step 157 (b123) put the CONVENTIONAL models on a generative footing:
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   isotropic Oort source, Galactic-tide injection, stellar remixing and
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   empirical discovery selection were required to produce the observed
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   arrival-direction distribution -- and failed (model in-cap fractions
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   ~0.25-0.28 against the observed 0.37-0.41).  Step 163 (b129) showed
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   the physically propagated discovery footprint cannot write the
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   observed dipole direction either.  The remaining asymmetry: the TEP
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   hypothesis itself has never been required to generate the data.  This
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   step applies the identical generative machinery to the TEP-side
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   models and asks what they predict.
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   The measured anomaly separates into two questions:
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   (i) Can the measured boundary slip REDIRECT arrival directions?
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   The fitted aphelion direction is what the catalogue records; if
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   the slip rotated it systematically toward the axis, an isotropic
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   arrival distribution could masquerade as the dipole.  The
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   step_151 injection transfer function measured the slip's effect
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   on fitted elements on the real observing chain -- its per-comet
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   fitted-aphelion displacement is applied here to synthetic
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   footprint-selected arrivals (M_slip), and the coherent
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   displacement that WOULD be required is computed directly (T4).
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   (ii) If the anomaly lives in the incoming state itself -- the
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   arriving population's source distribution -- what anisotropy
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   must the field write there?  Two morphologies are tested:
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   M_lobe (a localised sector enhancement, w propto 1 + A inside
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   the declared 60-deg cap) and M_dip (a bipolar modulation,
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   w propto 1 + m cos(theta_axis)).  The two are discriminated by
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   the anti-axis: M_dip depletes the far hemisphere, M_lobe does
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   not.  The observed anti-cap fraction decides.
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   T5 then checks the joint-consistency requirement on the real data:
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   the same axis-anchored structure must carry both the arrival
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   excess and the rotation field -- quantified as the rank
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   correlation between each comet's lobe weight and its measured
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   rotation, plus the inbound-leg asymmetry and flat energy channel
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   the downstream observables require.
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   Models (identical selection machinery to step_157)
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   M_iso      isotropic source x kappa(beta) selection  (control)
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   M_tide     tidal injection x selection               (conventional)
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   M_slip     isotropic x slip redirection x selection  (TEP boundary-
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   redirection realization)
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   M_lobe     isotropic x sector lobe x selection       (TEP source)
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   M_dip      isotropic x cos(theta) dipole x selection (TEP source,
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   bipolar morphology)
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   Inputs
[2026-09-21 15:44:51 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 164]   results/step_b28_bidirectional_rotation.csv   (arrival cohort)
